  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "The same formats as 0.1.0, read the same way, with the package now carrying its XML documentation and a skill beside the README. A JSON number answers TryToDecimal only where a decimal holds it exactly, which is a change of answer for a number beyond its precision or range. A JSON value nested as deep as the parser reads also writes back, compares and hashes, where those used to run out of stack. A TryParse that only answers whether reads the text once and builds no message, and an RFC 3339 timestamp is read without making a string of each field. Fixed: RFC 5322 refuses a dotted display name before an unclosed address (`a . a . a <b@c`) in linear time; it cost exponential time before — 41 seconds at twenty-two words. RFC 7239's Forwarded and RFC 8288's Link now refuse a long list with one bad element in memory proportional to the list's length, where it used to be quadratic — 1.17 GB refusing a 1,024-element Forwarded field, 414 MB for Link. Accepted input is read exactly as before in both cases.",
